          "question": "I keep thinking about killing myself and I don't know who to talk to.",
          "answer": "**Seek emergency care now.** What you have described can be a medical emergency. Call emergency services or go to an emergency department immediately. Do not wait to see whether it improves, and do not drive yourself.\n\n**This is an emergency. Please reach out for help now.** Thoughts of suicide are a reason to reach a person immediately, not to wait for a routine appointment (source: *Thoughts of suicide or self-harm*, red-flag guidance).\n\n- **If you might act on these thoughts, or you are in immediate danger, call your local emergency number now.** Do not leave yourself alone while you wait.\n- **In the US, call or text 988** to reach the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline. If you are in another country, look up your local crisis line now. The guidance notes that many countries run an equivalent service, and the numbers differ.\n- **Reach out to one trusted person today.** This could be a family member, friend, neighbor, coworker, or anyone nearby. You can say something simple, like: \"I'm having thoughts of killing myself and I need you to be with me.\" If you cannot think of anyone, the crisis line can help you work out who to contact.\n- **If you have a way you might hurt yourself, get it away from you or put distance between you and it.** Ask someone to help with this if you can.\n\nYou don't have to figure out who to talk to on your own. Calling or texting 988, or your local crisis line, is a good first step, and they can talk with you right now.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
